{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1195943-problems-with-mage-20-and-hacks-to-fix","id":1195943,"title":"Problems with Mage 20 and Hacks to Fix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-15T20:47:43-07:00","id":1195943,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Problems with Mage 20 and Hacks to Fix","content":"Hello Acolytes to Arch-Magi<br /> <br /> My Gm for a WoD game is interested in adding some mage aspects, but is worried about possible problems with the system and wants to try and predict to prevent them.<br /> <br /> So I'm asking for what issues there are in playing M20 and your hacks or house rules to get around them. <br /> <br /> It's Dark ages, for how that affects things, and will be a cross over, but that's a whole other kettle of fish; we're just looking at core system at this point<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:13:19-07:00","id":1196042,"title":"","content":"Are you using Pillars or Spheres?<br /> <br /> Because that's a pretty big difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:10:10-07:00","id":1196154,"title":"","content":"I've been writing a guide based on the difficulties I anticipate with running Mage 20. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZL4jPQpKjpjwIfMSi-UVbNq5jEgvLWS8VnXgNjY9SUU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZL4jPQpKjpjwIfMSi-UVbNq5jEgvLWS8VnXgNjY9SUU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZL4jPQpKjpjwIfMSi-UVbNq5jEgvLWS8VnXgNjY9SUU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZL4jPQpKjpjwIfMSi-UVbNq5jEgvLWS8VnXgNjY9SUU/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:05:21-07:00","id":1196263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1195943-problems-with-mage-20-and-hacks-to-fix?p=1196042#post1196042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you using Pillars or Spheres?<br /> Because that's a pretty big difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently neither.<br /> ST has a crazy idea to integrate Mage style magic (Whatever system that ends up being) in place of Blood sorcery for a Vampire game so it's more in line with his image of how it should work.<br /> We've mostly discussed Spheres and Arete system.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the complexity of the magic system and the... fluid nature of what can be done depending on the ST hasn't done it for me in the past. I prefer fixed rules for this power does this, then I can think of interesting ways to use it's effects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:16:08-07:00","id":1196266,"title":"","content":"Implementing the spheres without paradigm sounds like a recipe for powergaming free from roleplay. I'm not sure it's a good idea to lift the mechanics and ignore the themes that contextualise them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:20:46-07:00","id":1196270,"title":"","content":"If you're looking to play Mages with True Magick in the Dark Ages I highly recommend just playing Mage (or even Ars Magicka) rather than tacking it on Vampires. Trust me, it's better to try the game out as is before house rules and odd frankensystems.<br /> <br /> Just in case this wasn't totally clear I just want to make sure you know that this is the most helpful advice I can offer: don't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","user":"PazuzuAxelf","date":". 03-16-2018, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:26:27-07:00","id":1196274,"title":"","content":"Yeah... porting the Mage system to Vampire for a different blood magic system seems an entirely bad idea that goes way, way, beyond any simple rules issues or hacks for M20.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to do anything like that, I'd work on adapting Blood Sorcery from Requiem despite dealing with CofD vs. WoD rules, since the basic concepts of blood magic between the two games isn't that different, and Blood Sorcery's whole goal is to have simplified system for flexible blood ritual creation without going down the whole Mage rabbit hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T08:23:28-07:00","id":1196494,"title":"","content":"Another approach would be to take inspiration from the V20 Black Hand supplement, specifically its \u201cItarajana Sorcery\u201d. It's basically a nutshell version of <b>Dark Ages: Mage</b>'s Foundation-and-Pillars system, but written in the context of V20 and focused on a single Foundation and its Pillars. I'm not terribly familiar with <b>Vampire</b>; but I suspect that you could use this as a template to create alternate Foundations and Pillars to represent things like blood sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:22:26-07:00","id":1196649,"title":"","content":"I've found that in crossovers you should use a single system and have mechanical and thematic quirks.<br /> <br /> So take soak. All creatures soak the same way, but Vampires halve bashing damage after soak, as an example of a mechanical quirk.<br /> <br /> Take magical powers. Let's say your ST knows the Vampire system really really well. Vampires use Thaumaturgy, Mages use their &quot;Magick&quot; which is reskinned Thaumaturgy with reduced Difficulties, Werewolves can have &quot;Theurgy&quot; which mimicks a few Thaumaturgical paths and has many unique Rituals quickly stolen from the Werewolf system.<br /> <br /> It sadly loses a lot of what's special about each splat, but done well it can make for a very fun crossover. The alternative is the ST having to balance multiple systems, which can be a nightmare. In those cases each player should know their own mechanics like the back of their hand, and the ST needs to really, really trust them (by which I mean they only check if the Player is telling the truth occasionally, and use their best discretion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T14:31:48-07:00","id":1196905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1195943-problems-with-mage-20-and-hacks-to-fix?p=1196266#post1196266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Implementing the spheres without paradigm sounds like a recipe for powergaming free from roleplay. I'm not sure it's a good idea to lift the mechanics and ignore the themes that contextualise them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There would be a Paradigm, Tremere would be a blood soaked version of the Hermetics (of course)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative is the ST having to balance multiple systems, which can be a nightmare</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more worried about the players in this scenario, he's used to running over a dozen different systems. I think he has two nights a week he's not running a game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks everybody. I hope if I show the responces to him from mage regulars he'll change his mind (Because I like Thaumaturgy how it is personally) but as a player, I want my ST to be enjoying things as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}